{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Take the staff.</b> This is the staff of Aharon, as it is written here: ״ויקח משה את המטה מלפני ה׳״ — and this is the staff of Aharon, as it is written in the portion of Korah: ״השב את מטה אהרן לפני העדות למשמרת לאות לבני מרי״. And furthermore, the staff of Aharon was a sign for the children of Meri, and that is why Moshe said: ״שמעו נא המורים״. And Moshe already erred, for HaKadosh Baruch Hu said to him: ״take the staff״ — Moshe thought to strike the rock, but HaKadosh Baruch Hu did not say ״take the staff״ except because it was a sign for the children of Meri." "<b>And you shall speak to the rock.</b> This is what is called Miriam's well, which would flow water from itself and would roll along after Israel. And it is the rock that Moshe struck, which had not wanted to flow its waters on its account — because Miriam had died — and it returned in the merit of Moshe and Aharon, as our Rabbis explained in Ta'anit, as it is said: <b>ודברתם אל הסלע</b>. One may say that this matter is the same matter stated in the portion of Beshalah — but this is not so, for the incident of the Tzur was at Horev, while the incident of this rock was at Kadesh, at the edge of the land of Edom." "<b>And it will give its waters.</b> One may say: it will give drops, by means of speech." "<b>And you shall bring forth water for them.</b> Abundant, by means of striking with the staff. And therefore HaKadosh Baruch Hu commanded him to take the staff, and out of his agitation he did not remember to speak first, since in any event he had to strike it. And furthermore, because the rock had gone among the other rocks."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:49.703573614Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}